\" id=\"mwBAs\">Chinese sources</a> as the first of several <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Byzantine_emperor\" title=\"Byzantine emperor\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBAw\">Byzantine emperors</a> to send embassies to the Chinese <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Tang_dynasty\" title=\"Tang dynasty\" id=\"mwBA0\">Tang dynasty</a><sup about=\"#mwt331\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-halsall_2000_77-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;halsall 2000&quot;}}\"><a href=\"./Silk_Road#cite_note-halsall_2000-77\" id=\"mwBA4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBA8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBBA\">[</span>76<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBBE\">]</span></span></a></sup>","text":"Coin of Constans II (r. 641–648), who is named in Chinese sources as the first of several Byzantine emperors to send embassies to the Chinese Tang dynasty[76]"},"showInGallery":true,"srcset":[{"src":"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Solidus_Constans_II_%28obverse%29.jpg/330px-Solidus_Constans_II_%28obverse%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","scale":"1x"}]},{"title":"File:ForeignerWithWineskin-Earthenware-TangDynasty-ROM-May8-08.png","leadImage":false,"section_id":13,"type":"image","caption":{"html":"A Chinese <i id=\"mwBIo\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Sancai\" title=\"Sancai\" id=\"mwBIs\">sancai</a></i> statue of a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Sogdia\" title=\"Sogdia\" id=\"mwBIw\">Sogdian</a> man with a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Bota_bag\" title=\"Bota bag\" id=\"mwBI0\">wineskin</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Tang_dynasty\" title=\"Tang dynasty\" id=\"mwBI4\">Tang dynasty</a> (618–907)","text":"A Chinese sancai statue of a Sogdian man with a wineskin, Tang dynasty (618–907)"},"showInGallery":true,"srcset":[{"src":"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/ForeignerWithWineskin-E